0..75 Comment "// An equivalence between data types decided by computation, after the HoTT"
76..151 Comment "// book\'s § 2.10: a data type is covered as its constructors in tag order,"
152..229 Comment "// each applied to its fields\' patterns, so two maps that move fields between"
230..306 Comment "// constructors and back return every pattern, and `equiv` makes them a path"
307..374 Comment "// between the two types. Transport along the path applies the map."
376..453 Comment "// The shapes, the figures and `Shapes.toFigure`, the map from the one to the"
454..463 Comment "// other."
